{
 "id": "01a0fc4c-7886-7d91-b16b-c3b772a5691e",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (changed late Sept 2026, when Finance moved to a new accounting tool): plain comma-separated (`,`) with ISO dates `YYYY-MM-DD`. The previous tool needed `;` and `DD.MM.YYYY` (German locale); that no longer applies. UTF-8 without a BOM."
}
